  <body>
    <div class="example" id="strings">
      <h2><a href="./">F# by Example</a>: Strings</h2>
      
      <table>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            
          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            <a href="https://try.fsharp.org/#?code=zeRJfPqJ0BC"><img title="Run code" src="play.png" class="run" /></a><img title="Copy code" src="clipboard.png" class="copy" />
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="k">open</span> <span class="nn">System</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            <p>Strings are enclosed in double quotation marks (<code>&quot;</code>)</p>

          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="k">let</span> <span class="nv">a</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="s">&#34;This is a string&#34;</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            <p>You can use <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/fsharp/language-reference/strings">escape sequences</a> within a string, here we use a new line</p>

          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="k">let</span> <span class="nv">b</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="s">&#34;This is a string </span><span class="se">\n</span><span class="s">It&#39;s cool eh?&#34;</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            <p>You can create multi-line strings with triple quotation marks</p>

          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="k">let</span> <span class="nv">c</span> <span class="o">=</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">    <span class="s">&#34;&#34;&#34;
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="s">    This is a multi-line string
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="s">    1
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="s">    2
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="s">    3
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="s">    4
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="s">    &#34;&#34;&#34;</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            <p>F# gives us format specifiers similar to languages like C which specify the type of the data you wish you display
Here <code>%s</code> is saying &ldquo;I want to put a string here&rdquo;</p>

          </td>
          <td class="code">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="n">printfn</span> <span class="s">&#34;%s&#34;</span> <span class="n">a</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="n">printfn</span> <span class="s">&#34;%s&#34;</span> <span class="n">b</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="n">printfn</span> <span class="s">&#34;%s&#34;</span> <span class="n">c</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
      </table>
      
      <table>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            
          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="gp">$</span> dotnet fsi strings.fsx
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="go">This is a string
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="go">This is a string
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="go">It&#39;s cool eh?</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            
          </td>
          <td class="code">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="go">    This is a multi-line string
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="go">    1
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="go">    2
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="go">    3
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="go">    4</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
      </table>
      
      
